  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Dense image into a reduced scheme is schematically dense",
  "statement": "Let $X$ be reduced and let $h\\colon U\\to X$ be quasi-compact and\nquasi-separated with dense topological image. Then the image inclusion\n$\\operatorname{SIm}(h)\\hookrightarrow X$ is an isomorphism.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-dense-valuative/lemma-nagata-reduced-dense-image-schematic.md",
    "place": "node lemma-nagata-reduced-dense-image-schematic, order 276"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [
    "def-nagata-dense-compactification",
    "def-nagata-scheme-theoretic-image"
  ],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "On an affine open $\\operatorname{Spec}(A)\\subseteq X$, every element of the\nkernel ideal defining the scheme-theoretic image vanishes at every point of\na dense subset. It therefore lies in every prime ideal of $A$, hence in\nthe nilradical. Since $A$ is reduced, the element is zero. The kernel\nvanishes on an affine cover, so the image inclusion is an isomorphism.",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    }
  ],
